@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Overview of Cloud Computing";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Cloud computing is a technology that enables on-demand access to computing resources such as servers, storage, databases, networking, software, and analytics over the internet. It provides flexibility, scalability, and cost-effectiveness for businesses of all sizes.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-4">
        <p>
            Cloud computing allows users to access IT resources without maintaining physical hardware. It offers three primary service models—Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Software as a Service (SaaS)—each catering to different business needs.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h2>Key Benefits of Cloud Computing</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Scalability:</strong> Easily scale resources up or down based on demand.</li>
                <li><strong>Cost Efficiency:</strong> Reduces the need for costly on-premises infrastructure.</li>
                <li><strong>Flexibility:</strong> Access services from anywhere with an internet connection.</li>
                <li><strong>Security:</strong> Cloud providers offer advanced security features and compliance standards.</li>
                <li><strong>Automatic Updates:</strong> Ensures software and hardware are always up-to-date.</li>
                <li><strong>Disaster Recovery:</strong> Cloud-based backup solutions provide better business continuity.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://www.ibm.com/blogs/cloud-computing/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/cloud-computing.png" alt="Cloud Computing Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Cloud computing enables businesses to be more agile and efficient.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Types of Cloud Computing</h2>
        <p>Cloud computing is categorized into three major types:</p>
        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Public Cloud</h4>
                <p>Services provided by third-party cloud providers such as AWS, Azure, and Google Cloud, offering scalability and cost efficiency.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Private Cloud</h4>
                <p>Dedicated cloud infrastructure for a single organization, ensuring higher security and control.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <h4>Hybrid Cloud</h4>
                <p>A combination of public and private clouds, offering flexibility and optimized resource utilization.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Cloud Service Models</h2>
        <p>Cloud computing services are offered in various models to meet different business needs:</p>
        <table class="table table-bordered text-center mt-3">
            <thead class="table-dark">
                <tr>
                    <th>Model</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                    <th>Examples</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>IaaS</strong> (Infrastructure as a Service)</td>
                    <td>Provides virtualized computing resources over the internet.</td>
                    <td>AWS EC2, Microsoft Azure Virtual Machines</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>PaaS</strong> (Platform as a Service)</td>
                    <td>Offers a development platform with tools and frameworks.</td>
                    <td>Google App Engine, Azure App Services</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>SaaS</strong> (Software as a Service)</td>
                    <td>Delivers software applications over the internet on a subscription basis.</td>
                    <td>Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Salesforce</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Cloud computing has revolutionized the way businesses operate by offering cost-effective, scalable, and secure solutions. Whether utilizing **public, private, or hybrid cloud models**, organizations can optimize their resources, enhance collaboration, and improve business agility.
        </p>
        <p>
            As cloud technologies continue to evolve, businesses must adopt cloud strategies that align with their objectives to remain competitive and future-ready.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntroductionToMicrosoftAzure", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Introduction to Microsoft Azure &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>